# Scenarios 1 and 2: the workbench and the local Docker trial. No TLS, and one
# site on a port; with no host name in the address, that one block answers for
# handout.localhost and for every <address>.handout.localhost under it, which
# is what the application needs to hand out addresses that resolve.
#
# Both are the same file because nothing differs but the value: the workbench
# proxy in front of the first hands this Caddy its port through
# CADDY_SITE_ADDRESS, and compose.yaml sets it to :80 for the second, behind
# the published 8080.
{$CADDY_SITE_ADDRESS} {
	import handout-app
}
